# Even better: file-to-task mapping

This is the part you are describing.

```yaml
tasks:
  - id: task-001
    requirement: "Add pagination to user listing"
    
    files:
      - path: api/v1/users/list.mo
        role: endpoint
        status: pending

      - path: services/user.mo
        role: business_logic
        status: pending

      - path: repositories/user.mo
        role: data_access
        status: pending

      - path: testing/users/list_test.mo
        role: verification
        status: pending
```

But also maintain the reverse relationship:

```yaml
files:
  api/v1/users/list.mo:
    tasks:
      - task-001

  services/user.mo:
    tasks:
      - task-001
      - task-004

  repositories/user.mo:
    tasks:
      - task-001
```

So you effectively get a **bipartite graph**:

```text
             TASKS
               │
      ┌────────┼────────┐
      ↓        ↓        ↓
   task-001 task-002 task-003
      │        │        │
      └────┬───┘        │
           ↓            ↓
        FILES
           │
   ┌───────┼──────────┐
   ↓       ↓          ↓
service  repository  test
```

That is considerably more useful than a flat checklist.

