# Don't only track files — track evidence

This is where I would make LoopGoal significantly stronger.

Each task should have:

```text
Requirement
Affected files
Expected change
Actual change
Verification
Rule compliance
Evidence
Status
```

Example:

```yaml
task:
  id: task-001
  requirement: "Add pagination"

  files:
    - api/v1/users/list.mo
    - services/user.mo
    - repositories/user.mo
    - testing/users/list_test.mo

  evidence:
    api/v1/users/list.mo:
      changed: true
      verified: true

    services/user.mo:
      changed: true
      verified: true

    repositories/user.mo:
      changed: true
      verified: true

    testing/users/list_test.mo:
      changed: false
      verified: false

  status: incomplete
```

Now the AI cannot simply say:

> "I implemented pagination."

LoopGoal asks:

> **Show evidence for every mapped requirement.**

