# Skills and rules become another graph

Suppose your skill says:

```text
Controller
→ Service
→ Repository
→ Storage
```

and:

```text
Controllers must not contain business logic.
```

That should become:

```text
task-001
   │
   ├── file requirements
   │
   ├── skill requirements
   │    ├── controller rule
   │    ├── service rule
   │    └── repository rule
   │
   └── verification
```

Then the final check becomes:

```text
                 TASK
                  │
       ┌──────────┼──────────┐
       ↓          ↓          ↓
     FILES       RULES      TESTS
       │          │          │
       └──────────┼──────────┘
                  ↓
             COMPLIANCE
                  ↓
             PASS / FAIL
```

This is particularly important because your existing skills can contain architectural constraints, naming conventions, business rules, and verification requirements. 

