# The loop should become

```text
1. SCAN
   ↓
2. INVENTORY
   ↓
3. LOAD RULES + SKILLS
   ↓
4. ANALYZE GOAL
   ↓
5. BUILD TASK GRAPH
   ↓
6. MAP FILES
   ↓
7. EXECUTE ONE TASK
   ↓
8. RE-SCAN
   ↓
9. RECONCILE EXPECTED vs ACTUAL
   ↓
10. DISCOVER MISSING WORK
   ↓
11. UPDATE TASK GRAPH
   ↓
12. VERIFY
   ↓
13. CHECK SKILLS + RULES
   ↓
14. COLLECT EVIDENCE
   ↓
15. ALL REQUIRED ITEMS PASS?
       │
       ├── NO → continue
       │
       └── YES
             ↓
          FINAL AUDIT
             ↓
          COMMIT
```

### One important correction

Don't literally make it:

> "AI won't stop until everything passes."

Because that can create an infinite loop.

Make it:

> **LoopGoal will not declare completion until every required item has evidence of PASS, or the run reaches a bounded BLOCKED state.**

That gives you both **accuracy and safety**.

```text
PASS      → complete
FAIL      → fix
MISSING   → discover/fix
UNKNOWN   → investigate
BLOCKED   → stop safely with evidence
```

Never:

```text
UNKNOWN → PASS
```

